# Close-out B4 (M2-G3): POST /v1/cancel moves every not-yet-claimed (queued) item of the tenant's campaign to the terminal state cancelled, so nothing of it is ever claimed or pushed again. The fault makes the cancel step leave the queued items queued (the second statement's selector can match nothing). The real route is called over real HTTP against real Postgres with the real dispatcher ticking: every item must be cancelled with its two events and no send_logs row, none may be pushed to a worker, and a second tenant's un-cancelled campaign in the same ticks (the paired control) must still be claimed. The unpatched control passes; the patched run reports that the cancel did not cancel. Module 2's DB tests need a migrated template database, so the CMD builds one on the stock postgres service first, as tests/harness/run.sh does.
GATE=m2-cancel
TARGET=module:coldmail-send-managed
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestCancel_NothingNewIsClaimedOrPushedAfterCancel (the real cancel route, then the live dispatcher: nothing of the cancelled campaign is claimed or pushed, real Postgres)
CMD=T=fp_m2_p2c_tpl; TPL="${FAULT_ADMIN_DSN%/*}/$T"; psql "$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -q -c "DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS $T" -c "CREATE DATABASE $T" && psql "$TPL" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -q -c "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.users(id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), email text, is_active boolean default true, created_at timestamptz default now())" -c "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.job_items(id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), campaign_id uuid, user_id uuid, recipient_email text, rendered_subject text, rendered_body text, reply_to text, status text, created_at timestamptz default now())" && (cd tools/send-managed-migrate && go build -o bin/send-managed-migrate .) && MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL="$TPL" SEND_MANAGED_MODULE_PASSWORD=devmodulepass tools/send-managed-migrate/bin/send-managed-migrate up-and-set-password && cd services/control && TEST_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" TEST_TEMPLATE_DB="$T" SEND_MANAGED_MODULE_PASSWORD=devmodulepass go test -count=1 -v -run '^TestCancel_NothingNewIsClaimedOrPushedAfterCancel$' ./internal/dispatch/
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestCancel_NothingNewIsClaimedOrPushedAfterCancel
MESSAGE=want cancelled=4 in_flight=0 already_terminal=0
